From 74a929c253a163c4d977276861f9d981fc222ad7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:11:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sim): the rotary sweep states and can enforce its
 flute-rotation bound

The rotary chord pre-pass stands each sub-chord's tool on the mid pose,
so a tool point w from the reference is off its true-pose place by up to
w*2*sin(half/2). RotaryChordStats::flute_shift now states that bound
(L = farthest field-bounds corner from the tip, capped at shank + r);
with center_sag it is a two-sided Hausdorff bound on the chorded sweep.
Stock::simulate_rotary_bounded / ChordLaw::flute_tol also enforce it
(more sub-chords, refused by name past MAX_SUBCHORDS); simulate_rotary
keeps its count and output.

Agreement suite stock_rotary_flute: field vs a brute-force sampled
reference (4,001 poses of the controller's lerp), 0 sign misses past
the stated bound and past an enforced 0.05 mm; the sag class alone
misses by 9.5e-3, so the bound is the one covering the flute.

Fixes #20

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
